window.products.push({"id":963551,"name":"Windlass Hand Forged Medieval Iron Eating Cutlery Set with Leather Belt Pouch Case - Viking Feastware","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":38.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71EZ0DpBDqL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"Banquets and feasts were a time of celebration in medieval times. And this hand-forged cutlery set is a perfect accessory. Finally, feasting utensils for the re-enactor on the go! Great for Viking and medieval settings, our knife, fork, and spoon set fit neatly in a tie-fold, open belt leather pouch for a great combo. Easy to take along to the fair, a picnic, camp out, or wherever you want to be able to eat out! The handle for each hand-forged piece has the traditional blacksmith's twist and the knife is capable of holding an edge. Each piece is approximately 8\" long overall. A leather Pouch for carrying is included. Please clean before use; these have been heated treated and oil quenched. Caring for Iron Cookware and Utensils Our authentic cooking utensils, cutlery, eating utensils, pots, pans, kettles are made with the same materials and in the same way, the originals were made. Perfect for re-enactment, from Roman encampments to Viking and Medieval camps, feasts, and festivals, your settings will be authentic! To get years of use from forged iron cookware and utensils we recommend the following steps. How To Season Your Iron Utensils: Scrub well in hot soapy water Scrub well in hot soapy water Dry thoroughly Dry thoroughly Spread a thin layer of melted shortening or vegetable oil over the skillet. Spread a thin layer of melted shortening or vegetable oil over the skillet. Place it upside down on a middle oven rack at 375° (Place foil on a lower rack to catch drips) Place it upside down on a middle oven rack at 375° (Place foil on a lower rack to catch drips) Bake 1 hour and let cool in the oven Bake 1 hour and let cool in the oven Cast Iron Upkeep: Rinse with warm water and use a brush or scraper to remove stuck-on bits Rinse with warm water and use a brush or scraper to remove stuck-on bits For really stuck-on food, scrub with salt and oil, rinse and wipe clean For really stuck-on food, scrub with salt and oil, rinse and wipe clean Dry the pan and coat with a thin layer of oil Dry the pan and coat with a thin layer of oil Store until ready to use Store until ready to use","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71EZ0DpBDqL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Windlass","source_asin":"B00BAMJMEM","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-963551","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00BAMJMEM","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B00BAMJMEM","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
